  "id": "tax.us.2025.rule.sli-worksheet",
  "notes": "2025 Student Loan Interest Deduction Worksheet (i1040gi.pdf p.99), lines 2-9, publishing Schedule 1 line 21. Track 0 T0-4/T0-9 settlement (docs/phases/engine-breadth/milestones/f1098e-student-loan-interest-agi.md); repaired at Track 4b (docs/phases/engine-breadth/milestones/f1098e-student-loan-interest-agi.md, Track 4b). Line 1 is read by ref from tax.us.2025.sli-worksheet.line1-total-interest-paid-subtotal, published by the sibling rule.sli-worksheet-line1-subtotal.json -- this rule never collects the family itself, since ADR-0016's audit_collect_authority requires a rule that collects a mapped family to publish exactly that family's authorized subtotal, and this rule publishes a different (final worksheet) symbol; mirrors the f1099g.1 / rule.f1099g-1-subtotal.json / rule.schedule1-line7.json three-rule cascade shape exactly. Track 4b repair: that sibling subtotal is now the family's RAW, uncapped closure-authorized sum (the true ADR-0016 authority object -- what the closed family attests exists, never a downstream computation), because tying the Schedule 1 attachment's itemization to a pre-capped subtotal falsely blocked any filer whose true box-1 interest exceeded $2,500 (packages/derivation/runner.py's itemization tie-out requires the raw member row-sum to equal the pinned subtotal_symbol exactly). This rule now applies the worksheet's own $2,500 line-1 cap itself, via the min(a,cap)=a-max(a-cap,0) idiom (tax.us.2025.parameter.sli-interest-cap), at every point it reads worksheet line 1: once feeding the final 'line1 minus line8' subtraction and once feeding the 'line1 times line7' multiplication that produces line 8 -- both sites now read the capped value, never the raw subtotal symbol directly, so the worksheet's own dollar arithmetic is byte-identical to before this repair for every input; only which rule owns the cap changed. Line 3 (the worksheet's 'total of Schedule 1 lines 11-20, 23, and 25') is a literal 0: T0-5 confirms Part II is purely additive and none of those twelve lines has a producer in this codebase yet, so their contribution is honestly 0 whenever the twelve Schedule-1-native absence facts (reused unchanged from schedule1-adjustments-scope.bundle.json, never re-minted) are confirmed 'yes'; a 'no' on any of them means this return has an adjustment this milestone cannot compute, and blocks SLI_SCHEDULE1_PART_II_OUT_OF_SCOPE rather than silently treating line 3 as 0. Line 5's threshold and line 7's phase-range divisor are filing-status-keyed parameters (mirrors tax.us.2025.f1098.mortgage-interest-limit's shape); line 7's ratio uses the new divide op (rule-artifact.v6, min_decimal_places 3, half_up) then is itself capped at 1.000 with the same min(a,cap)=a-max(a-cap,0) idiom this rule now also uses for line 1's own $2,500 cap (Track 4b). Line 8 uses the new multiply op. The final dollar amount is rounded once under the project rounding.convention, matching rule.ss-benefits-worksheet.v2's own outer-round placement -- the divide op's own min_decimal_places floor is a distinct, earlier precision floor on the ratio itself, never overridden by this final whole-dollar round. Eligibility: require_closed on the Form 1098-E box-1 family is unconditional (this route is optional at the return level, matching rule.schedule1-line10.json's path-dependency shape, T0-9 point 5 -- never a when-guarded requires). The twenty-two count>0-conditional components (T0-2 components 2-4, 5-7/9-10, the twelve Schedule-1-native absences, and the two legal-zero components 11-12) are gathered via conditional_dependency_set exactly as rule.ss-benefits-worksheet.v2 already does for its own twenty-two conjuncts (T0-9 point 2) -- never all, which short-circuits and would silently fail to report every absent component at once. filing_status (component 1, MFS exclusion) stays outside that set and unconditionally required: ADR-0038 forbids a conditional member whose fact type is named in a category_literal unless that fact type declares the {yes,no} domain, and tax.us.2025.filing-status declares five statuses, exactly the same reasoning rule.ss-benefits-worksheet.v2 already documents for its own unconditional filing_status read. The MFS check itself reads the bare 'filing_status' choice symbol (not tax.us.2025.filing-status, a different string) on its ref left-hand side, exactly mirroring rule.ss-benefits-worksheet.v2's own no-rrb-adjacent filing_status categorical_compare shape: the ref names the symbol the run marshals as 'filing_status'; category_literal's fact_type.id is the domain identity used only for the categorical-domain-match check. Component 8 (box 2 not checked, T0-3) has no pin and is never read here: tax.us.2025.f1098e.box2-checked-authority's own value_schema admits only null/false, and tax.us.2025.f1098e.box1-student-loan-interest is registered as its companion-presence pair (packages/tax/loader.py domain_companion_presence_pairs), so a checked box 2 is rejected at kernel admission before any box-1 finding bearing it could ever become current -- pinning a value this rule never reads would fabricate an audit trail (ADR-0007 decision 4). The count==0 (closed-empty family) route returns literal 0 without evaluating any of the eligibility checks, reading the line-1 subtotal, or the worksheet's own arithmetic, mirroring rule.ss-benefits-worksheet.v2's identical count==0 shortcut: an empty, closed family already makes line 1 (and hence the whole worksheet) 0 for every filing status and every MAGI, so none of filing_status's MFS exclusion, the twenty-two conditional components, or the worksheet's own line 2-8 arithmetic can change the answer and must not gate it. On the nonempty route, MFS blocks SLI_MFS_INELIGIBLE; a 'no' on any of the ten T0-2 universal components (2-4, 5-7, 9-10) blocks SLI_UNIVERSAL_COMPONENT_VIOLATION (never a silent zero, never a silent full-box-1 pass-through, per Track 0 adversarial closure artifact 2); a 'no' on either legal-zero component (11-12) computes an explicit 0, never a block; otherwise the full nine-line worksheet computes. Track 6b repair (docs/phases/engine-breadth/milestones/f1098e-student-loan-interest-agi.md, Track 6b): Track 6's path (j) found the five per-statement universal witnesses (5-7/9-10: no-related-person-interest, no-qualified-employer-plan-interest, no-non-qualified-loan-component, no-employer-educational-assistance-interest, no-qtp-earnings-used) were read via a single unkeyed `ref` per fact-type-id, so packages/derivation/marshal.py bound only one arbitrary current finding on a multi-statement family, making the SLI_UNIVERSAL_COMPONENT_VIOLATION disposition depend on assertion order rather than on whether any statement actually violates. Fixed by removing these five from the top-level conditional_dependency_set's members (an unkeyed ref's own env.symbols binding is no longer populated once the fact type is registered as a collect source name with more than one current finding, so a plain `ref` there would wrongly block DEPENDENCY_ABSENT on every legitimate multi-statement return) and reading each witness instead with the new collect_categorical_all_equal op (rule-artifact.v6, additive), which reads every current finding for that fact type from the marshalled source rows (never env.symbols) and requires all of them to answer 'yes' -- a true 'no member violates' universal test, independent of assertion order. The five witness fact types are registered as collect source names (packages/derivation/live.py); packages/derivation/marshal.py's binding loop was also hardened so an unkeyed symbol with two or more current findings that is NOT a collect source name is left unbound (ordinary DEPENDENCY_ABSENT) rather than arbitrarily bound to one of them. Track 3/4's own single-statement worksheet arithmetic is unaffected: a lone current finding for a witness fact type still yields exactly one source row, so collect_categorical_all_equal returns the same True/False the prior ref+categorical_compare conjunct did.",
